 Why: The compiler owns the closed policy registry and its scope rules
 Fix: Use `gc`, `explicit_units`, `copies: .Explicit`, `writes: .Explicit`, `failures: .Explicit`, or `sentries: .Off`; write memory floors as `!Mem.*` effect denials
